1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:09,250
Carlos Guentes wrote, the orange tree is a traveling tree, a natural witness to all human follies.

2
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:16,110
The tree is the lush, beautiful fruit of the earth, of what is original and essential.

3
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:21,350
And the earth, continues, Guentes, is different from the world.

4
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:30,570
The world passes away, but the earth endures and will always take care of us if we allow it to survive.

5
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:42,290
And that, he says, is the purpose of both literature and life itself, to assure that life goes on, that life does not end.

6
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,390
The story is left unfinished.

7
00:00:44,910 --> 00:01:05,650
This celebration of black girls at this magical, magic ball that we, my dear brothers and sisters, are remembered and endure like the earth.

8
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:16,610
So I say to you, calling all women, men, children, students, black girls, calling all oceans, skies, clouds, trees, black girls.

9
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:21,630
This is a peace journey, black girls, magic ball, black girls.

10
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:25,030
This is an anthology called peace.

11
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:39,050
No assassins allowed, no wars allowed, no greed allowed, no bullying allowed, no killings allowed, no arguments allowed, no gossip allowed, no homophobia allowed, no racism allowed.

12
00:01:39,050 --> 00:02:05,170
Here, just the slow, quick smell of peace and justice and black girls everywhere, sliding from our tongues, our hands, our eyes, calling all journeymen and journeywomen to this journey of words of churches, schools, universities, homes, countries, cities, of banks and corporations, congress and senate courtrooms and courtyards,

13
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:15,430
of the white house, prisons and hospitals where men and women sometimes genuflect skeletons, calling all peace warriors and black girls.

14
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:20,530
Let us genuflect peace, black girls, every day, black girls.

15
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:23,550
Peace is a human right.

16
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:25,970
Tony Morrison said we die.

17
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:31,130
That may be the meaning of life, but we do language.

18
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,950
That may be the measure of our lives.

19
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:50,650
And my dear sisters, how you do this thing, how you do this thing called life, how you anoint our eyes for surprise and beauty as you bring us into the flesh of rain and laughter called peace, called black girls.

20
00:02:50,650 --> 00:03:09,290
How you do this thing, how you do this thing, called peace and justice and love, love, love, love, love, love, love, love, love.

21
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:27,710
So I say to you, my dear sisters, on this festive occasion, on this beautiful occasion, on this occasion where we honor each other and our soul, come, come, come, come, come, come, come, come, come, come, come.

22
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:44,880
Let us flush the world's flesh with peace and love, with peace and love, and live, you black girls all over the world.

23
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:50,700
Just live, live, live, live, live, live, live, much love to you.

24
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:54,560
Every while I was thinking about the day, how am I going to do today?

25
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:59,040
And I think that's one of the things that I attempt to do.

26
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,680
I attempt to wear my days well.

27
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:05,840
And I want people to learn how to wear their days well.

